## Root causes filed

### 1. Parser Issue — 393 reports

**GitHub Issue #11**: [#4471: Parser issue (393 reports) — month-first parser, day-first tenants](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/11)

The shared date parser reads all dates with month first. Tenants in day-first locales type dates as DD/MM, but the parser interprets them as MM/DD, causing consistent inversion across app (186), email (159), and form (48) channels.

**Root cause**: Parser not locale-aware.

**Affected locales**: en-GB, en-IE, it-IT, fr-FR, de-DE, nl-NL, da-DK, pt-PT, es-ES, pl-PL, cs-CZ

---

### 2. Hint Issue — 34 reports

**GitHub Issue #12**: [#4471: Hint issue (34 reports) — form misleads day-first users](https://github.com/OldMetalmind/s01e03-ticket-4471/issues/12)

Booking form v3 shows "MM/DD/YYYY" hint to all users. Day-first users (de-DE, es-ES, pt-PT) type DD/MM as they naturally would, but the form parses it as MM/DD, flipping the date.

**Root cause**: Form hint hardcoded, not locale-aware.

**Affected tenants and reports**:
- alder.physio (de-DE): 12
- copper.studio (es-ES): 11
- pale.harbour (pt-PT): 11

---

